load @term/seed/structure/set
  find set

# A grammar: a finite set of rules for generating the strings of a language, the syntax half of computation. The Chomsky
# hierarchy ranks grammars by power: regular (recognized by finite automata), context-free (by pushdown automata),
# context-sensitive (by linear-bounded automata), and unrestricted (by Turing machines, the full computable languages).
# Each rung recognizes strictly more languages than the last. The form carries the set of symbols; the production rules
# and the start symbol are the grammar, and the automaton that recognizes each class is in the automaton folder.
form grammar
  link symbols, like set
